      propertyPath: title
      value: Magnitude = length
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: 'Appart from defining the independend dimension offset, vectors can
        be defined with a direction and a length, also known as the magnitude.


        The
        length can be calculated using Pythagora''s theorem.


        For 2D:

        square
        root(x*x + y+y)


        For 3D:

        square root(x*x + y*y + z*z)


        This 
        pattern continues for more dimensions.


        Note that the because of
        the squaring, the result is always positive.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
