    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: title
      value: Metallic
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: 'When looking at how light actually interacts with surfaces, there is
        a difference between metals and non-metals.


        For metals, the light
        can either be reflected or absorbed. How much depends on the incoming light
        angle and material and is described by the fresnel effect.


        If the
        surface is rough, the light is reflected in different ways. In addition,
        the geometry can mask itself which influences how light is reflected. These
        Microfacets aren''t modelled but instead described statistically with a roughness
        term. Instead of calculating it perfectly, different approximation functions
        exist.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
