      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'Meshes are made of triangles. Drawing a wireframe that highlights the
        edges of each triangle helps visualize these.


        Doing so requires
        to know how far away from the edge a fragment is. The standard mesh data
        usually doesn''t give this information. However, this data can be added in
        the geometry shader. The new order is:

        vertex -> geometry -> fragment


        We
        give each point an independent barycentric coordinate. The interpolation
        between the geometry and fragment shader means we can use this coordinate
        to determine the distance from the edge.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
