    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: title
      value: Geometry shader
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: 'Modelling a separate grass mesh often doesn''t make much sense. It''s
        a lot of work, there is a huge amount of data to be stored and the performance
        also suffers. Doing so on the CPU also isn''t great.


        Therefore,
        drawing the grass around the player at runtime on the GPU makes most sense.
        This can be done in the geometry shader by adding new vertices to the mesh.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
