    - target: {fileID: 3686973092905522621, guid: 3b78f404deb68354e9b08eaf5d093c61,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: title
      value: Parallax occlusion mapping
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3686973092905522621, guid: 3b78f404deb68354e9b08eaf5d093c61,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: "Textures often look flat when looking at them. Very often, light models
        are used to make them look more interesting. Another method however is Parallax
        occlusion mapping (aka POM). \n\nWhen the surface has large height differences,
        looking at it from different sides causes different sides of the surface
        details to be shown. POM simulates this by using a displacement map, using
        raymarching in the view direction to find the intercept point and then sampling
        the texture at the right point.\n\nRaymarching is also further explained
        in the Math section."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3686973092905522621, guid: 3b78f404deb68354e9b08eaf5d093c61,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: linkedMaterial
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 2100000, guid: a82e162718b6504418fc5cb87275bee4, type: 2}
