    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: title
      value: Multiple Unity lights
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: 'As mentioned with the single light, the BIRP (Built in render pipeline)
        only processes one Unity light  per pass.


        However, only 2 need
        to be defined. First, the ForwardBase pass is calculated, which also includes
        the ambient light and reflection probe. The second pass that needs to be
        defined is tagged ForwardAdd. This is evaluated for every additional light.


        Again,
        note that doing it this way is out of date outside of Unity BIRP and modern
        rendering pipelines sample the light sources differently.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
