    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: 'The depth buffer indicates how far things are away from the camera.
        For opaque shaders, this value is usually calculated automatically and written
        into the depth pre-pass, which the GPU skip the fragment function if for
        anything that is behind it.

        However, it is also possible to write
        to the depth buffer directly. Doing so usually breaks this optimization though.'
