    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: title
      value: AlphaToMask
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1055789876787810633, guid: 7ffcca573e1296d47a9191342db0701b,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: 'Simply discarding pixels often causes very sharp edges with aliasing
        issues at the pixel border. AlphaToMask allows a blending if Anti-Aliasing
        is enabled.


        Note: The result will depend on your Anti-Aliasing
        level and apparently your graphics card.

        - For Nvidia cards, the
        output seems to be differnt layers of transparency.

        - For AMD Graphics
        cards, the output seems to be dithered, meaning you can see individual pixels
        despite Anti-Aliasing.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
