    - target: {fileID: 3686973092905522621, guid: 3b78f404deb68354e9b08eaf5d093c61,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: 'Usually, shaders don''t have access to the previous state. Howevere,
        having so would be very useful, since it would allow for cool programs. That''s
        why render textures exist.


        In this simple example, the texture
        can be made to melt by merging the current pixel value with the value above.
        The resulting render texture is then displayed like a normal texture.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
