    - target: {fileID: 3686973092905522621, guid: 3b78f404deb68354e9b08eaf5d093c61,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: title
      value: Celular automata
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3686973092905522621, guid: 3b78f404deb68354e9b08eaf5d093c61,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: 'In 1970, John Horton Conway came up with Conway''s Game of Life. To
        calculate the next state, each cell looks at its own an 8 neighbors to deterimine
        the next state:

        - If alive and <2 live neighbors = dies

        -
        If alive and 2 or 3 live neighbors = stay alive

        - If alive and >
        3 live neighbors = dies

        - If dead and 3 live neighbors = born

        From
        this simple rules, different shapes display different properties, algorythms
        can be created (it''s turing complete) and given enough space, it is thought
        that even life could emerge from a large enough random field.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
